---
description: Keep routine work in the harness and expose only useful product details.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Let the harness handle routine work

Applies to product design, implementation and review across UI, orchestration,
setup, settings and user-facing errors.

If the system knows the next step and can safely perform it under existing
authority, the harness owns it.

- Implement routine retries, reconnection, lease maintenance and finalization in
  the owning service. Do not turn orchestration gaps into user checklists.
- Each control and detail must enable a real decision, resolve uncertainty or help
  use a result. Keep incidental internal states and identifiers out of default views.
- Keep normal operation quiet. Show brief, contextual status only when useful,
  backed by observed server state. Never hide blockers or imply progress that has
  not occurred.
- Do not ask task users to certify infrastructure facts.

**Review:** Check that harness responsibility is implemented, visible details
serve a purpose the user should affect.

Apply this rule to changed flows; unrelated redesign is not required.
